void on_data_processed(const BusEvent *e) {
    total_bytes += e->payload.bytes_processed;
}
```

**Sub-bug C2 — `total_bytes` is a local variable, not a file-scope (static) or shared variable:**
```c
// main.c  — BROKEN
void on_data_processed(const BusEvent *e) {
    size_t total_bytes = 0;                    // re-initialized on every call!
    total_bytes += e->payload.bytes_processed;
    // total_bytes dies here; the summary can never see it
}
```
**Fix:** Declare `total_bytes` at file scope (or pass it in via a context pointer) so it persists across calls and is readable when the summary is printed:
```c
// main.c  — FIXED
static size_t total_bytes = 0;   // file-scope: survives across callback invocations

void on_data_processed(const BusEvent *e) {
    total_bytes += e->payload.bytes_processed;
}

// ... later, in the summary:
printf("Total bytes processed: %zu\n", total_bytes);
```

