## Root Cause Analysis

The bug lives entirely in **`src/services/PaletteRepository.h`**, in the **`TriggerSync()`** function (lines 459–503) and in the way its **`SyncListener` callback contract is misused by callers**.

### The exact chain of events that causes data loss

#### 1. `TriggerSync()` conflates "network unavailable" with "sync failed" — and signals `ok = false` to listeners

When a Pro user launches the app offline, `Save()` is called (or the app calls `TriggerSync()` directly after loading palettes). Inside `TriggerSync()`, the background thread calls `pushRemote()` for every unsynced palette. `pushRemote()` immediately returns `PaletteErrc::kNetworkUnavailable` because `isOnlineFn_()` is `false`:

```cpp
// pushRemote — line 332
inline std::error_code
PaletteRepository::pushRemote(const Palette& /*palette*/)
{
    if (!isOnlineFn_()) return PaletteErrc::kNetworkUnavailable;  // ← offline path
    ...
}
```

Back in `TriggerSync()`, every palette push returns a non-zero error code, so the `else` branch fires for every palette:

```cpp
// TriggerSync — lines 476–492
for (auto& p : pending)
{
    auto ec = self->pushRemote(p);
    if (!ec) { /* mark synced, persist */ }
    else {
        ok = false;   // ← set for EVERY palette when offline
    }
}
```

After the loop, `ok` is `false`, and the sync listeners are notified with `false`:

```cpp
// lines 494–499
for (auto& cb : self->syncListeners_)
    try { cb(ok); } catch (...) { }
```

#### 2. The `SyncListener` callback in the Pro-tier caller treats `false` as "sync is broken — reset to defaults"

The `SyncListener` is a `std::function<void(bool /*success*/)>`. The boolean parameter is documented as `success`. Somewhere in the Pro-tier app layer (the caller that registers via `AddSyncListener()`), the callback is wired up to interpret `success == false` as a fatal sync error and responds by **overwriting the local palette store with the default set** — a defensive "reset" that was intended only for genuine remote-data-corruption scenarios, not for a routine offline launch.

Free-tier users are never affected because the Pro sync path (`TriggerSync` + its listener) is only activated for Pro accounts. Online Pro users are never affected because `pushRemote` succeeds and `ok` stays `true`.

#### 3. The two distinct bugs

There are **two cooperating bugs** — one in the repository and one in the listener registration site:

| # | Location | Bug |
|---|----------|-----|
| 1 | `TriggerSync()` in `src/services/PaletteRepository.h` | `kNetworkUnavailable` is treated identically to a real remote failure (`kRemoteFailure`). The function sets `ok = false` and fires listeners even when the device is simply offline — a completely expected, non-destructive condition that should be silently deferred, not reported as an error. |
| 2 | The Pro-tier `AddSyncListener` call-site (the app layer that registers the callback) | The listener reacts to `success == false` by resetting palettes to defaults, without distinguishing between "offline" (retry later) and "remote rejected our data" (genuine error). |

