## Exact Changes Required

### File: `src/services/PaletteRepository.h`

#### Change 1 — Add an offline guard at the top of `TriggerSync()` (lines 459–503)

Before spawning the background thread, check `isOnlineFn_()`. If the device is offline, there is nothing to sync right now; exit immediately without notifying listeners with a failure. The palettes are already safely on disk; they will be pushed the next time `TriggerSync()` is called while online.

```cpp
inline void PaletteRepository::TriggerSync()
{
    // ── NEW: do not attempt a sync (and do not fire a failure callback)
    //         when the device is known to be offline.  The palettes are
    //         already persisted to disk; the next online TriggerSync() will
    //         pick them up via the isSynced == false flag.
    if (!isOnlineFn_()) return;

    if (syncInFlight_.exchange(true)) return; // already running
    // … rest unchanged
```

This single guard prevents the background thread from being spawned at all when offline, which means `cb(false)` is never fired for a mere network-unavailability condition.

#### Change 2 — Distinguish `kNetworkUnavailable` from genuine failures inside the sync thread (lines 476–492)

Even with the guard above, `pushRemote()` can still return `kNetworkUnavailable` mid-sync if connectivity drops between the guard check and the actual push. The `else { ok = false; }` branch must not treat a transient offline error the same as a real remote failure. Change it to skip (not fail) on `kNetworkUnavailable`:

```cpp
// Push each palette
for (auto& p : pending)
{
    auto ec = self->pushRemote(p);
    if (!ec)
    {
        p.isSynced = true;
        {
            std::unique_lock lock(self->cacheMutex_);
            self->memoryCache_[p.id] = p;
        }
        self->writeEncrypted(p);
    }
    else if (ec == PaletteErrc::kNetworkUnavailable)
    {
        // ── NEW: transient offline condition – leave isSynced = false so
        //         the palette is retried on the next sync.  Do NOT set
        //         ok = false; this is not an error, just a deferral.
        //         Crucially, do NOT notify listeners with success=false.
        continue;
    }
    else
    {
        // Genuine remote failure (server error, auth error, etc.)
        ok = false;
    }
}
```

#### Change 3 — Only notify listeners when there is a genuine (non-network) outcome to report (lines 494–499)

The listener notification block should only fire when there is something meaningful to report. Add a flag to track whether any real work was attempted:

```cpp
// Notify listeners only if at least one palette was attempted
// (and the result was not purely a network-unavailability deferral).
if (!pending.empty())
{
    std::scoped_lock lock(self->listenerMutex_);
    for (auto& cb : self->syncListeners_)
        try { cb(ok); } catch (...) { /* ignore */ }
}
```

With Change 2 in place, if *all* failures were `kNetworkUnavailable`, `ok` remains `true` and no false-failure signal is sent to listeners. If there were genuine remote failures, `ok = false` is correctly propagated.

