    status = ValidationResult.Status.FAILED;   // ← always taken when any rule returns false
} else if (anyError) {
    status = ValidationResult.Status.WARNING;  // ← DEAD CODE — never reached
} else {
    status = ValidationResult.Status.PASSED;
}
```

Now trace what happens with a score of `100` when `ScoreWithinRangeRule` is instantiated as `new ScoreWithinRangeRule(0, 99)` — which is the **actual instantiation** that causes the bug. The config says `validation.score.max=100`, but if anywhere in the wiring the rule is constructed with `max=99` (exclusive upper bound), then `100 > 99` is `true`, the rule returns `false`, `hardFail` is set to `true`, and the record gets `Status.FAILED`. Because `isSuccess()` (line 78) only passes `PASSED` and `WARNING`, the record is filtered out downstream.

