|---|---|---|
| `src/config/app.config.ts` | `defaultPostValues.status` | Change `'PUBLISHED'` → `'DRAFT'` |
| `src/core/services/user.service.ts` | `savePost` (or equivalent) spread merge | Move `...defaultPostValues` **before** `...postData` so caller-supplied values win |

Both changes may be needed, or only one depending on which was introduced in the refactor — but the spread-order bug in `user.service.ts` is the direct mechanical cause of the caller's `'DRAFT'` being silently discarded, and the wrong default in `app.config.ts` is the latent value that replaces it. Fixing the spread order alone is sufficient to stop drafts from being published; fixing the default value as well is the correct defensive measure so that posts with no explicit status are never accidentally published.

